cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this project, cite the repository and record the commit and access date. Citation does not grant data reuse rights."
type: software
title: "New York Times Headline Analysis (2000–2025)"
authors:
  - family-names: "KASIGAZI"
    given-names: "OLIMI EMMANUEL"
    website: "https://olimiemma.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/olimiemma/NYT-analysis-2K-2K5"
url: "https://github.com/olimiemma/NYT-analysis-2K-2K5"
abstract: >-
  Independent Python data engineering and natural language processing case study
  of New York Times article metadata from 2000 through 2025. Includes data quality
  auditing, TF-IDF, VADER lexical sentiment, sampled spaCy named-entity recognition,
  and visualizations. Raw data is not distributed. An optional RAG prototype has
  incomplete setup. The project is not affiliated with The New York Times Company.
keywords:
  - natural language processing
  - data engineering
  - data quality
  - headline analysis
  - journalism
  - Python
